{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778544820777,"sessionID":"ses_1e68c71dcffeNqJwmNMee1uYLT","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-a79ecfad37f07422","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"src/ontology/cl.Makefile","limit":100,"offset":100},"output":"<path>/home/runner/work/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/src/ontology/cl.Makefile</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n100: \n101: # FBbt mapping set\n102: $(MAPPINGDIR)/fbbt.sssom.tsv: .FORCE\n103: \twget -O - \"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/fbbt/fbbt.sssom.tsv\" | \\\n104: \t\tsssom-cli --prefix-map-from-input \\\n105: \t\t          --include 'object==CL:*' \\\n106: \t\t          --update-from-ontology $(SRC):object,label,existence \\\n107: \t\t          --output $@\n108: \n109: # ZFA mapping set (extracted from ZFA cross-references).\n110: # ZFA does contain oboInOwl:treat-xrefs-as-... annotations, but here\n111: # it's easier to ignore them, as this automatically filters out all the\n112: # xrefs that point to anything else than CL.\n113: # 1. Create intermediate set from ZFA.\n114: $(TMPDIR)/zfa.sssom.tsv: .FORCE | all_robot_plugins\n115: \t$(ROBOT) sssom:xref-extract -I http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/zfa.owl \\\n116: \t\t                    --mapping-file $@ -v --drop-duplicates \\\n117: \t\t                    --ignore-treat-xrefs \\\n118: \t\t                    --map-prefix-to-predicate 'CL https://w3id.org/semapv/vocab/crossSpeciesExactMatch' \\\n119: \t\t                    --set-id http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/zfa/zfa.sssom.tsv \\\n120: \t> $(REPORTDIR)/xfa-xrefs-extraction\n121: \n122: # 2. Create definitive ZFA set by checking against CL's contents\n123: $(MAPPINGDIR)/zfa.sssom.tsv: $(TMPDIR)/zfa.sssom.tsv $(SRC)\n124: \tsssom-cli -i $< --update-from-ontology $(SRC):object,label,existence,source -o $@\n125: \n126: endif\n127: \n128: # Mappings component\n129: # ------------------\n130: # The mappings.owl component is derived from the remote mapping sets\n131: # (as fetched above). It contains old-style cross-references to make\n132: # those mappings \"visible\" to CL editors and users in the usual way.\n133: $(COMPONENTSDIR)/mappings.owl: $(SRC) $(EXTERNAL_SSSOM_SETS) | all_robot_plugins\n134: \t$(ROBOT) sssom:inject -i $< \\\n135: \t\t\t      $(foreach set, $(EXTERNAL_SSSOM_SETS), --sssom $(set)) \\\n136: \t\t\t      --ruleset $(SCRIPTSDIR)/mappings-to-xrefs.rules \\\n137: \t\t\t      --error-on-unshortenable-iris \\\n138: \t\t\t      --no-merge --bridge-file $@ \\\n139: \t\t\t      --bridge-iri http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/cl/components/mappings.owl\n140: \n141: \n142: # ----------------------------------------\n143: # TAXON CONSTRAINTS CHECK\n144: # ----------------------------------------\n145: \n146: # The TC check requires te taxslim-disjoint-over-in-taxon.owl ontology,\n147: # which is declared as an ODK mirror (under the name ncbitaxondisjoints)\n148: # and as such should already have been downloaded into the mirror\n149: # directory by the standard ODK-generated rule. But the QC checks are\n150: # typically run under MIR=false, so while the standard rule would be\n151: # invoked by Make it would not result in the mirror being downloaded.\n152: # So instead, we make the TC check depend on another file, and here we\n153: # 1. force the download of the mirror if it is not already there;\n154: # 2. create a link to that mirror.\n155: $(TMPDIR)/taxslim-disjoint-over-in-taxon.owl:\n156: \tif [ ! -f $(MIRRORDIR)/ncbitaxondisjoints.owl ]; then \\\n157: \t\t$(MAKE) $(MIRRORDIR)/ncbitaxondisjoints.owl MIR=true IMP=true ; \\\n158: \tfi && \\\n159: \tln -f -s ../$(MIRRORDIR)/ncbitaxondisjoints.owl $@\n160: \n161: # Actual TC check: we add the taxon disjointness axioms into the\n162: # ontology, make sure to expand all macros, then try to reason over the\n163: # resulting product.\n164: $(REPORTDIR)/taxon-constraint-check.txt: $(EDIT_PREPROCESSED) $(TMPDIR)/taxslim-disjoint-over-in-taxon.owl\n165: \t$(ROBOT) merge $(foreach src,$^,-i $(src)) \\\n166: \t\t expand -o $(TMPDIR)/cl-plus-taxon-disjoints.ofn \\\n167: \t\t reason -r WHELK > $@\n168: \n169: # Include the TC check in the routine tests\n170: test: $(REPORTDIR)/taxon-constraint-check.txt\n171: \n172: \n173: # ----------------------------------------\n174: # OTHER CUSTOM CHECKS\n175: # ----------------------------------------\n176: \n177: .PHONY: obocheck\n178: obocheck: $(SRC) | all_robot_plugins\n179: \t$(ROBOT) merge -i $(SRC) \\\n180: \t\t remove --base-iri $(URIBASE)/CL_ --axioms external --trim false \\\n181: \t\t convert --check false -f obo $(OBO_FORMAT_OPTIONS) \\\n182: \t\t         --output $(TMPDIR)/cl-check.obo\n183: \tfastobo-validator $(TMPDIR)/cl-check.obo\n184: \n185: test_obsolete: $(ONT).obo\n186: \t! grep \"! obsolete\" $<\n187: \n188: test: obocheck \\\n189:       test_obsolete\n190: \n191: \n192: # ----------------------------------------\n193: # TAXON SUBSETS\n194: # ----------------------------------------\n195: \n196: TAXON_ID_human = NCBITaxon:9606\n197: TAXON_ID_mouse = NCBITaxon:10090\n198: \n199: # Create a taxon-specific subset. This rule creates two distinct files:\n\n(Showing lines 100-199 of 401. Use offset=200 to continue.)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"\n# FBbt mapping set\n$(MAPPINGDIR)/fbbt.sssom.tsv: .FORCE\n\twget -O - \"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/fbbt/fbbt.sssom.tsv\" | \\\n\t\tsssom-cli --prefix-map-from-input \\\n\t\t          --include 'object==CL:*' \\\n\t\t          --update-from-ontology $(SRC):object,label,existence \\\n\t\t          --output $@\n\n# ZFA mapping set (extracted from ZFA cross-references).\n# ZFA does contain oboInOwl:treat-xrefs-as-... annotations, but here\n# it's easier to ignore them, as this automatically filters out all the\n# xrefs that point to anything else than CL.\n# 1. Create intermediate set from ZFA.\n$(TMPDIR)/zfa.sssom.tsv: .FORCE | all_robot_plugins\n\t$(ROBOT) sssom:xref-extract -I http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/zfa.owl \\\n\t\t                    --mapping-file $@ -v --drop-duplicates \\\n\t\t                    --ignore-treat-xrefs \\\n\t\t                    --map-prefix-to-predicate 'CL https://w3id.org/semapv/vocab/crossSpeciesExactMatch' \\\n\t\t                    --set-id http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/zfa/zfa.sssom.tsv \\","truncated":true,"loaded":[]},"title":"src/ontology/cl.Makefile","time":{"start":1778544820767,"end":1778544820775}},"id":"prt_e198836d4001PWrdy6Blzvnl3y","sessionID":"ses_1e68c71dcffeNqJwmNMee1uYLT","messageID":"msg_e19883014001137xMxMaY1yZCq"}}
